Done. **Final CV: SMAPE 4.1793** (fold-2018, full-year-ahead extrapolation; expanding-year folds 2016/2017/2018 = 5.02/4.84/4.18).

**Pipeline result:**
- Baseline naive lag-364: 10.05. LGB raw log1p: 8.43 (trees can't extrapolate level).
- **GDP normalization** (World Bank gdp_pc per country-year, incl. 2019): LGB on log(num_sold/gdp_pc) 5.80, -2.6 SMAPE.
- **Structural Ridge won** — log1p multiplicative decomposition (country/store/product/dow dummies, Fourier k6×product, eoy×country, log_gdp + linear year trend): 5.53. Confirms experience-library dichotomy: shares constant across years (store ratio 1.742 every year) means structure beats GBDT.
- **Biggest lever**: per-holiday-name × offset dummies. Residuals showed +3..+7 days post-Easter/Midsummer misses (+34%); widening window to -5..+10: 5.46 → **4.19**.
- Final: 0.95 ridge + 0.05 lgb_gdp, rounded to int, retrained on all 2015-2018.

